A||||4||SCCA FIERO||Are 86-87GT deck vents different from 88GT vents?||||1||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||12-29-2001||05:33 PM||||I converted my 88 Coupe to a fastback a couple years ago. The notchback vents are totally different, I knew that. After all this time I finally found the brackets to hold the fastback vents for an 88GT (The brackets that hold the screws to remove the vents). Problem is now I have 86GT vents and mounting for 88GT vents and the holes for the screws are about 1/2 an inch too far in for the screws to go in. <P>I guess what I need to know is if the mounting holes in the vents are located in different places from 86-87 to 88.<P><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||12-29-2001||06:58 PM||||I really don't know.  The only 1988 Fiero I have is a Coupe.  So why am I posting?<P>Strangely enough, each vent cover on my '88 Coupe has 2 holes for the (one) inboard hold-down fastener - the holes are about a half inch apart - roughly the same mismatch you mention.  So, in other words, on each cover, there's one outboard hole, and there're 2 inboard holes, 1/2-inch apart.<P>I don't know if these are the original equipment covers, whether someone used older-model covers from salvage and drilled the extra holes, or what.  Maybe GM decided to add the extra inboard holes so they'd be good for '88 and pre-'88 cars?  <P>Kind of suggests you might be able to use the covers you already have, and add an inboard hole to each, to match the '88 strut tower / bracket location?<P>That's really all I know.  Hope it helps in some way.||||reg||5
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||12-29-2001||09:55 PM||||86 - 88 are all the same for GT's.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-29-2001||09:56 PM||||My 87 and 88 GTs have the same vents.  I imagine the 86s are the same as the 87.  How the brackets mount to the space age for the coupe and fast back may be different.  Since I don't have a coupe, don't know.||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Aura||12-30-2001||01:35 PM||||In 88, the mounting bracket for the vents that bolts ontothe  strut tower changed. It became smaller, neater and less complicated.<BR>You could just re-drill the holes in the '86 vent to fit the 88' mounting bracket pattern.<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips, Cross Drilled Rotors||||reg||1
